OpenCode Go Widget for Debian/Ubuntu
===================================

The package installs two halves:

  /usr/lib/opencode-go-widget
      GTK app: API key, polling and desktop card
  /usr/share/gnome-shell/extensions/ocg-usage@local
      Panel ring, weekly label and dropdown

Enabling the panel extension
----------------------------
GNOME Shell only scans extension directories at session start, so log out and
back in once after installing. Then start "OpenCode Go Widget"; at startup it
enables the bundled extension automatically. It leaves the extension disabled
if you have explicitly disabled it in the Extensions app.

Until that next login the app uses the tray-icon fallback.

Start the app
-------------
Launch "OpenCode Go Widget" from the app grid, open Settings, paste your
OpenCode Go API key and press Test connection, then Save. The key is stored
per user in ~/.config/opencode-go-widget/token (mode 0600).

Autostart is off by default. Enable "Start automatically at login" in
Settings.

Removing the package
--------------------
Before removing the package, clean up the per-user state:

  opencode-go-widget --uninstall

This quits the widget, disables the panel extension, and removes the autostart
entry and cache. Add --purge to also delete the API key and settings:

  opencode-go-widget --uninstall --purge

Then remove the package:

  sudo apt remove opencode-go-widget

The same cleanup is available from Settings -> Uninstall....
